            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "MATHEMATICS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.138,
            0.901,
            0.176
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(vi) Five years hence, the age of Jacob will be three times that of his son. Five years ago, Jacob’s age was seven times that of his son. What are their present ages?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.193,
            0.382,
            0.213
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.3.2 Elimination Method"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.219,
            0.902,
            0.278
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now let us consider another method of eliminating (i.e., removing) one variable. This is sometimes more convenient than the substitution method. Let us see how this method works."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.292,
            0.902,
            0.352
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 8 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The ratio of incomes of two persons is 9 : 7 and the ratio of their expenditures is 4 : 3. If each of them manages to save ` 2000 per month, find their monthly incomes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.357,
            0.902,
            0.417
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let us denote the incomes of the two person by ` 9x and ` 7x and their expenditures by ` 4y and ` 3y respectively. Then the equations formed in the situation is given by :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.391,
            0.422,
            0.898,
            0.442
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "9x - 4y = 2000\\tag{1}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.448,
            0.142,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.392,
            0.447,
            0.897,
            0.468
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "7x - 3y = 2000\\tag{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.094,
            0.473,
            0.902,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 1 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Multiply Equation (1) by 3 and Equation (2) by 4 to make the coefficients of y equal. Then we get the equations:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.366,
            0.517,
            0.898,
            0.538
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "27x - 12y = 6000\\tag{3}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.368,
            0.544,
            0.898,
            0.564
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "28x - 12y = 8000\\tag{4}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.57,
            0.901,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 2 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Subtract Equation (3) from Equation (4) to eliminate y, because the coefficients of y are the same. So, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.219,
            0.615,
            0.618,
            0.635
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "(28x - 27x) - (12y - 12y) = 8000 - 6000"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.642,
            0.14,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.45,
            0.641,
            0.547,
            0.659
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "x = 2 0 0 0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.666,
            0.574,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 3 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Substituting this value of x in (1), we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.341,
            0.692,
            0.547,
            0.712
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "9(2000)-4y=2000"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.718,
            0.139,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.45,
            0.718,
            0.546,
            0.737
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_20.jpg",
          "content": "y = 4 0 0 0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.742,
            0.901,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the solution of the equations is x = 2000, y = 4000. Therefore, the monthly incomes of the persons are ` 18,000 and ` 14,000, respectively."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.793,
            0.901,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Verification :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 18000 : 14000 = 9 : 7. Also, the ratio of their expenditures = 18000 – 2000 : 14000 – 2000 = 16000 : 12000 = 4 : 3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.845,
            0.216,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Remarks :"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.868,
            0.902,
            0.909
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. The method used in solving the example above is called the elimination method, because we eliminate one variable first, to get a linear equation in one variable."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
